  "cx": {
    "_note": "CX beys are assembled, so no single row of the catalogue is 'the blade'. A bey's name is its lock chip plus the one blade it is built around — 天馬爆擊 / Pegasus Blast is the Pegasus chip on the Blast main blade — so `beys` names those two pieces per blade key and the sheet shows their weights side by side rather than summed. The over blade and the assist blade are separate parts with their own weights above, and are deliberately not counted here; the sheet says so. Keys are the catalogue's blade `key` (the base Chinese name), so every colour variant and metal coating of one mould inherits it. The pairing is read off the Chinese name rather than the English, which is wrong for two rows — see the README note below.",
    "plasticChipG": 1.7,
    "_chipNote": "Every plastic lock chip weighs the same, so only the two metal ones are listed. A chip absent from `metalChips` is plastic and takes `plasticChipG`.",
